    <meta name="description" content="Standing at 828 meters with 163 floors, the Burj Khalifa in the United Arab Emirates is the world's tallest building. Explore its Y-shaped structural design inspired by Islamic architecture, the USD 1.5 billion construction story by SOM and Emaar Properties, observation decks on the 124th and 148th floors, luxury Armani Hotel, residential apartments, sustainability features, and what makes this Dubai icon an enduring case study in modern architectural ambition.">
        
